or promote any kind of behavior;
viewer discretion is advised]

5
00:00:10,660 --> 00:00:11,680
Can you call me that again?

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,600
You called me "Soul."

7
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,240
You took really nice pictures.

8
00:00:16,320 --> 00:00:17,920
You're even prettier
in person than in the photo.

9
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,680
So, I think...

10
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,560
I actually might really like you, Mim.

11
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,400
You look after me, take care of me,
pay attention to me...

12
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,040
That's what you'd call flirting.

13
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,160
So, can I?

14
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,040
Lately,

15
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,760
you're the only one in my life.

16
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,520
Oh, Mom?

17
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:48,960
Soul, dear.

18
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:54,540
I'm going to a meditation retreat
with Phing in Saraburi for three days.

19
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:57,040
What, Mom? Why so suddenly?

20
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:59,380
Well, we were just talking

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,520
and decided just like that.

22
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,640
Wow...

23
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,180
Are you gonna be okay on your own?

24
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,740
Of course I am, Mom.

25
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,200
I'm all grown up now.

26
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:10,800
You don't have to worry about me.

27
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,660
I know you say that,

28
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,600
but I still worry.

29
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,280
But...

30
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,640
I'm just as stubborn as you.
I love sneaking out, too.

31
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,800
Anyway, don't forget to
eat all your meals,

32
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,040
and don't stay up too late, dear.

33
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,040
Understood, Mom.

34
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,640
Oh,

35
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,600
if you're free,

36
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,980
don't forget to visit Xinxin, too.

37
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,480
Go keep her company.

38
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,600
Phing is also worried about her,

39
00:01:37,880 --> 00:01:39,400
and I'm worried about you.

40
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:43,160
If you two stay together,
then we can both stop worrying.

41
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,120
I haven't talked to her in a week, Mom.

42
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,200
She's probably busy

43
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,200
and doesn't have time to see anyone.

44
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,000
Are you two fighting or anything?

45
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,200
We're probably not.

46
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:02,360
We were talking just fine before this.

47
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,420
Or maybe...

48
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:10,040
Judging by what she said,

49
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,340
she was definitely hitting on you, girl.

50
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,600
If I were you, I wouldn't
even question it anymore.

51
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:16,900
Her words, her actions,

52
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,200
anyone can see she's hitting on you.

53
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:20,820
Well, I mean,
you can't help but wonder, right?

54
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,140
If I assume she's hitting on me,

55
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:23,880
she'll just think I'm full of myself.

56
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,880
Is my sweet little Xinxin
finally falling in love?

57
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,120
- Lada!
- I'm gonna cry.

58
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,760
I'm being serious!

59
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,000
Alright, listen.

60
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,020
If she likes you,

61
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:37,880
you'll know it.

62
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,880
But if she doesn't,

63
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,000
you'll be confused.

64
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,680
So sharp, so on point.

65
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:45,140
How did you even think of that, girl?

66
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:45,980
I picked it up somewhere.

67
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,020
Gosh!

68
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,520
I almost had a heart attack.

69
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,720
You could ask the whole world,

70
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,240
but no one would know better

71
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,840
than you

72
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,500
and your Miss Architect.

73
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,560
Alright, sweetie?

74
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,360
She isn't my Miss Architect.

75
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,440
So many words, but they all mean

76
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:05,280
"my Miss Architect."

77
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:07,620
You only focused on that word, huh?

78
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:09,120
Nothing else in your life matters anymore?

79
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:10,400
Gosh...

80
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:13,680
Can you two take this more seriously?

81
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,680
Who isn't being serious here?

82
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:16,680
- You, sis.
- You, sis.

83
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,720
Gosh!

84
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:23,400
Well, from what Lada said,

85
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,280
I have just one question.

86
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,180
Do you even know

87
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,920
that she likes you?

88
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,680
Well, I know,

89
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,900
but I'm just not sure

90
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,180
if she was

91
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,720
actually... hitting on me

92
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:39,560
or just being friendly...

93
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,840
But you're the closest person to her.

94
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:46,780
You're the one who would

95
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,000
pick it up.

96
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,260
But from what you've told us,

97
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,240
I think...

98
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,800
you really mean a lot to her.

99
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,560
If you weren't that important,

100
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,140
she wouldn't leave her meeting...

101
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,360
just to see you. Am I right?

102
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,140
True. I agree with her on this.

103
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:03,120
And you have to ask yourself

104
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,300
why you didn't call Nan or me that day,

105
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,680
but chose to call her first.

106
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,740
This is so obvious. Super obvious.

107
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,080
It's because

108
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:16,600
she's your top priority
right now, isn't she?

109
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:17,680
Hm?

110
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,660
Well...from what we've discussed,

111
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:25,240
if you still don't have the answer,

112
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:27,580
I think you should take some time apart.

113
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,560
No meeting up, no talking at all.

114
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:30,940
And if you still

115
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,800
miss her,

116
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,440
that means

117
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,420
you already like her, Xinxin.

118
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,400
It's alright.

119
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,560
It's gonna be okay.

120
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:29,600
Soul.

121
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,760
Are you alright?

122
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,040
You've been playing with your food
for like half an hour now.

123
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:37,080
Yeah, he's right.

124
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,060
It's nothing.

125
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,560
I don't feel like eating.

126
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,000
And what's the matter?

127
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,040
You're wearing the unlucky color again.

128
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,320
What does lioness mean?

129
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,560
- Huh?
- Huh?!

130
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,140
What does lioness mean?

131
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,640
Well, someone told me that...

132
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:04,520
I'm a lioness.

133
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,280
Lioness.

134
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,760
I see.

135
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,320
Let me guess.

136
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,260
Is it something like

137
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:16,600
a lady-killer?

138
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:18,720
But "lady-killer"

139
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:20,720
is used to describe guys who play around.

140
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:23,040
If they called you that,

141
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,500
you're a woman who plays around.

142
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,320
What?

143
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:27,400
- Really?
- Mm.

144
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:28,480
Do I look like one?

145
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,880
You don't.

146
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:33,840
Because if you were one,

147
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,420
you'd already have someone, right?

148
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:36,060
Yeah.

149
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,860
Ever since I've known you,

150
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:40,080
I haven't heard about anyone at all.

151
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,700
Yeah, she's right.

152
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,040
You can believe her.

153
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,720
Someone like Mim, you know...

154
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,280
She's always attentive

155
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,000
and likes to know what's going on.

156
00:07:48,020 --> 00:07:50,060
So, if there's anything she doesn't know,

157
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,200
it doesn't exist.

158
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,560
Hey.

159
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,480
- Oyl.
- What?

160
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:57,960
Hold on.

161
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:01,320
If someone said
you're like...a lady-killer,

162
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,920
that means...

163
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,380
your flirting skills

164
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,840
are quite something, huh?

165
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,760
That's also true.

166
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,380
See?

167
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,960
Who says only tigers hide their claws?

168
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:13,860
- Here!
- Mm.

169
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,000
"A lioness hides her claws."

170
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,400
Gosh...

171
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:19,660
I'm just following my feelings, you know?

172
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,280
You don't really need any skills for that.

173
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:24,140
And...

174
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,160
why do you...

175
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:27,960
look so down

176
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,680
like this?

177
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:30,960
They don't like you?

178
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:34,440
I don't even know if she liked me.

179
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,400
She just totally ghosted me.

180
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:43,580
I don't wanna think about it anymore.

181
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,760
My head's killing me.

182
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:45,900
- Whoa.
- What?

183
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,120
Wait, Soul.

184
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,640
What's wrong with her?

185
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,460
She hasn't even eaten yet,
and now she's gone.

186
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,720
Honestly, sis,

187
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,780
what a waste of shrimp.

188
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,040
Yeah. Then why didn't you...

189
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,780
eat it?

190
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,020
- You're right.
- Hey, hey!

191
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,040
Oh, my bad.

192
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,760
Hello, Madam Waen.

193
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,720
You couldn't reach her at all?

194
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:34,880
Well...I'll go look for her, then.

195
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,880
Alright.

196
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:38,720
Goodbye.

197
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:50,200
Oh, it's not that bad. I'm fine.

198
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,020
- Nope.
- How are you getting back, though?

199
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:53,240
Want to take my car?

200
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:55,480
No worries,
someone's gonna pick me up.

201
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:10,500
Who's that, Soul?

202
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:19,560
Xinxin!

203
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:22,920
Lada!

204
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:24,760
How did you get here?

205
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:25,900
And...

206
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,280
how did you get here?

207
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,260
So, Ms. Xinxin was

208
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,000
the feng shui master who worked with you.

209
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,820
And she's also your friend?

210
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,760
So Soul is your architect?

211
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:44,220
She isn't my architect.

212
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:49,540
So, Ms. Xinxin was the one

213
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:51,440
who called you a lady-killer, right?

214
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:53,040
What?

215
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,420
Have you been gossiping about me?

216
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,680
Hey, don't worry about me right now.

217
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,360
Let's talk about these two.

218
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,280
What's the deal?

219
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:04,000
She was still your client
just last month, wasn't she?

220
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,080
Hey...

221
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,220
Hey...

222
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,520
What's the deal?

223
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,160
Spill.

224
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,200
Uh...

225
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:13,840
I'll tell you about it later.

226
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,100
Yeah, right, right.

227
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,820
Aren't you feeling under the weather?

228
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:19,880
You'd better go get some rest.

229
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,840
Well, I need to get back to work.

230
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,680
I have to go now, Ms. Xinxin.

231
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:26,040
Uh...

232
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,060
Goodbye, Soul.

233
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:28,920
I gotta go.

234
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:42,880
So...

235
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:45,080
are you feeling that bad?

236
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,960
I just have a slight fever.

237
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,220
But don't tell my mom about it.

238
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:53,160
I bet she'll rush out of the temple
if she finds out.

239
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,080
Whoa...

240
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:15,800
you made this yourself?

241
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:17,440
Nope.

242
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:19,040
I ordered it.

243
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,560
I knew it.

244
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:22,760
I doubt

245
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,640
you'd go to the trouble of cooking for me.

246
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:26,820
Just eat it already,

247
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,560
so you can take your meds
and get some sleep.

248
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:31,600
How can I sleep
when my work isn't done yet?

249
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:34,080
A little rest won't hurt.

250
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,640
You can take a break too, you know.

251
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:39,040
We work to earn money

252
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,760
for trips,

253
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,960
not to spend it on
medical bills like you do.

254
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,340
You're nagging just like my mom.

255
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:53,160
So, why are you here anyway?

256
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,400
Did you need something?

257
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,600
Oh...

258
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,960
Madam Waen called me

259
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:59,640
and said she couldn't reach you.

260
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:02,400
Maybe she doesn't know you're sick.

261
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,520
Right,

262
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,560
I'll call her back.

263
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:09,200
Sorry for

264
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,080
causing you so much trouble.

265
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,640
It's fine.

266
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:17,040
We're working together anyway.

267
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:29,480
So...

268
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,240
are you heading back now?

269
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,640
It's going to get late.

270
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,840
Are you alright by yourself?

271
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:38,660
Oh, it's nothing.

272
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:40,280
I'll just take some meds and...

273
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:04,960
Whoa...

274
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,080
You're burning up.

275
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:10,100
If you were alone, you could’ve
hit your head on the floor

276
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,440
and passed out in your house.

277
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,140
It's not that bad.

278
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:16,360
I'll just take some meds, and I'll be fine.

279
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,580
Medicine won't help

280
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:20,920
if you don't get some rest.

281
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,520
Didn't you say

282
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:24,320
you were taking good care of yourself?

283
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,860
Going to bed early

284
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:27,360
and not pushing yourself too hard...

285
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:29,760
How did you get sick, then?

286
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:32,780
There's just too much work,

287
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,160
and I can't get it all done in time.

288
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:39,080
Then why did you take on this project?

289
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,580
Why didn't you just let Mr. Pat handle it?

290
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:44,600
How did you know?

291
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:47,560
Ms. Mim told me everything.

292
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,280
When?

293
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:54,500
Well, Soul is a bit under the weather,

294
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:56,380
so I took her to the doctor.

295
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,600
Then I dropped her off here.

296
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,320
Luckily, it wasn't anything serious.

297
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:03,120
Why did she suddenly get sick?

298
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,440
Well, Soul has been
working really hard lately.

299
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:10,040
She took on Madam Waen's project for Pat.

300
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:13,400
He's a senior architect at the company.

301
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:16,580
Normally, the most...

302
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:17,520
she'd take on is...

303
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:19,640
around...three projects.

304
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,100
But then Madam Waen's project came along,

305
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,320
and it really threw her off.

306
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,820
If she was handling this many projects,

307
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,760
why didn't she let someone else handle it?

308
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:34,840
I think it was because of you.

309
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,760
I'm not trying to gossip, but...

310
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,120
You are.

311
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:45,380
This isn't "gossiping,"

312
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,920
it's a "warning."

313
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,600
Well, if you happened

314
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,520
to work with Pat,

315
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:57,800
I bet he'll be flirting with you nonstop.

316
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,300
Even Oyl, who's an expert flirt,

317
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,160
can't compete with him.

318
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:04,360
This person

319
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,640
is a total lady-killer.

320
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:10,240
You're in for a bumpy ride
if you have to work with him.

321
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:13,300
I think Soul was worried about you,

322
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:14,660
so she took on this project instead.

323
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,600
Gosh, Mim...

324
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:25,920
If you're struggling,

325
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:28,720
just let Mr. Pat
handle this project instead.

326
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,000
Don't push yourself this much.

327
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,000
No.

328
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:36,520
I want to work with Mr. Pat.

329
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:39,320
At least I don't have to argue with him
like I do with you.

330
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:41,740
I already took on the project,

331
00:16:41,760 --> 00:16:43,040
so I have to finish it.

332
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,240
And I won't let you

333
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,680
work with anyone else either.

334
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:55,000
You're not the only architect
in this world, you know.

335
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:59,560
But the only feng shui master
I want to work with

336
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,320
is you, Xinxin.

337
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:22,680
Cheers.

338
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,960
I just found out that
the architect Xinxin talked about

339
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,320
is your senior at work.

340
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,080
What a small world, huh?

341
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:38,960
Do you think...

342
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,320
your senior

343
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,520
likes my friend?

344
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:49,920
What about your friend?

345
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,700
Does she like my senior?

346
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,120
Well, I can't speak

347
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,280
for her.

348
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:08,480
But there's no doubt

349
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:11,920
that I like you.

350
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:18,640
You like me that much, huh?

351
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:21,500
What about you?

352
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:25,400
What?

353
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,000
Do you like me?

354
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,920
So much.

355
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:44,540
Just...

356
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:45,640
go to sleep.

357
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:47,640
I'll be sleeping downstairs.

358
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:49,100
What?

359
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,660
You can sleep in my room.

360
00:20:50,680 --> 00:20:52,200
Why do you want to go downstairs?

361
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,660
You said you'd look after me,

362
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,480
so shouldn't you be
keeping a close eye on me?

363
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:58,600
Are you really sick?

364
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:00,540
Do you wanna see the doctor's note?

365
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:01,640
I'm just being sarcastic.

366
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,960
Come on, just sleep in my room.

367
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,680
I'm too weak to do anything to you.

368
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:09,800
You pervert!

369
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:13,160
Come on.

370
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:26,040
You're the one who told me
to go to bed early, come on.

371
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:39,360
Do you...

372
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,920
usually go to bed early?

373
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:43,000
Well...

374
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:46,360
I try to go to bed before midnight.

375
00:21:48,160 --> 00:21:49,140
Then...

376
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:51,520
until Madam Waen's project is finished,

377
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:53,360
text me

378
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,880
before you go to bed, okay?

379
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,800
Why do you care when I go to bed?

380
00:22:02,080 --> 00:22:04,120
So I can go to bed.

381
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,320
How so?

382
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:09,980
Well, when you text me,

383
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,440
I'll know it's time.

384
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,500
Sometimes I get so caught up in work

385
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:16,280
I completely lose track of time.

386
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:21,960
You're saying that like
you'll believe what I say.

387
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,400
What?

388
00:22:23,580 --> 00:22:26,400
Why don't you try it before judging?

389
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,920
Let's start today, then.

390
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,640
It's already past 10.

391
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:36,000
Time to call it a night, Miss Architect.

392
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,360
Aww...

393
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:39,160
Can we make it 11?

394
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:39,980
See?

395
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:42,060
We haven't even started,
and you're already negotiating.

396
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:44,120
Then why should I even tell you?

397
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:48,700
Alright, take it easy.
Don't snap at me yet.

398
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,120
I'm gonna sleep, alright?

399
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:53,000
I'm not even snapping.

400
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:55,960
I've never snapped at you.

401
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:58,720
You were the one who snapped at me

402
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,700
when we first met.

403
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:06,100
I'm sorry

404
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:09,520
for leaving you with
a bad memory of our first meeting.

405
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,920
But from now on,

406
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:15,960
I'll make things better.

407
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:23,520
It's too late to feel sorry now,
Miss Architect.

408
00:23:24,040 --> 00:23:25,120
You were such

409
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,960
a grumpy, loud lion back then.

410
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,140
Wait...

411
00:23:37,160 --> 00:23:38,620
I'm going to sleep now.

412
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:41,760
Can you turn off the lights for me?

413
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:44,640
And...

414
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:48,000
that love-boosting lamp you bought for me...

415
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,360
Shouldn't that be turned off?

416
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,240
I think...

417
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,960
it's starting to work now.

418
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:15,920
Sweet dreams, Xinxin.

419
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:48,320
Morning.

420
00:24:49,140 --> 00:24:50,280
Morning.

421
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:54,800
Why are you looking at me like that?

422
00:24:56,240 --> 00:24:57,120
So pretty.

423
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:08,560
Why the puzzled look?

424
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:11,720
How could you tell?

425
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:15,220
Well, you've got that
confused puppy look on your face.

426
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:17,840
Hey... A dog? Really?

427
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,840
What's not cute about dogs?

428
00:25:22,140 --> 00:25:23,100
You're right.

429
00:25:23,780 --> 00:25:25,220
I like dogs,

430
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:27,640
and I like you, too.

431
00:25:33,580 --> 00:25:35,180
So, what do you want to know,

432
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:35,920
huh?

433
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:38,980
I'm just thinking...

434
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,960
where do we go from here?

435
00:25:42,920 --> 00:25:44,480
We've come this far.

436
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:46,200
Wasn't last night clear enough?

437
00:25:49,360 --> 00:25:50,600
It was,

438
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:53,140
but I mean our status.

439
00:25:54,320 --> 00:25:55,600
Well...

440
00:25:57,040 --> 00:25:58,160
why don't we make it official?

441
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:00,560
Of course.

442
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:02,000
What are we waiting for?

443
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:03,400
So, we're girlfriends now, huh?

444
00:26:03,560 --> 00:26:04,440
Mm.

445
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:06,040
We are,

446
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:07,320
babe.

447
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:12,680
Does that mean
I can do whatever I want with you?

448
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:26,480
Can I have more, please?

449
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,280
Go on.

450
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:30,720
I'm your girlfriend,
so I can do whatever I want.

451
00:26:35,510 --> 00:26:37,280
You're not allowed to leave me now.

452
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:39,680
You got that? Huh? Huh?

453
00:27:09,240 --> 00:27:10,120
Hey.

454
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:12,240
Hey...

455
00:27:16,320 --> 00:27:16,800
Hey.

456
00:27:18,580 --> 00:27:19,580
Why are you spacing out?

457
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:22,600
I'm not.

458
00:27:25,840 --> 00:27:28,600
I've already cancelled
my meeting with the client today.

459
00:27:28,960 --> 00:27:29,840
I don't think...

460
00:27:30,020 --> 00:27:32,240
I'll get everything done in time.

461
00:27:32,560 --> 00:27:33,200
What?

462
00:27:33,840 --> 00:27:34,760
Why?

463
00:27:34,780 --> 00:27:36,320
Do you have something to do today?

464
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:38,320
Well, it's you.

465
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,040
You're such a troublemaker.

466
00:27:41,480 --> 00:27:42,320
I...

467
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:43,640
ordered some congee.

468
00:27:43,920 --> 00:27:45,640
Do you want some?
I'll heat it up for you.

469
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,040
What, aren't you gonna eat with me?

470
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,960
I...already ate

471
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,800
before you came down.

472
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:55,960
Well, last night

473
00:27:56,220 --> 00:27:57,360
we went to sleep at the same time,

474
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,400
so we have to wake up together,

475
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:01,000
and then have

476
00:28:01,140 --> 00:28:03,740
breakfast together, like...

477
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:04,440
Stop it!

478
00:28:04,800 --> 00:28:05,900
Don't you say it.

479
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,080
Go sit and wait for me.

480
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:15,480
Go.

481
00:28:18,540 --> 00:28:19,720
Okay.

482
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:40,040
Come sit with me.

483
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:43,000
I told you I already had breakfast.

484
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:46,060
I'm not asking you to eat.

485
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:48,240
I just want you to sit with me.

486
00:28:50,680 --> 00:28:51,960
Please?

487
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:16,920
Come on, hurry up and eat,

488
00:29:17,020 --> 00:29:18,000
so you can take your meds.

489
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:20,000
Then I can finally go home.

490
00:29:20,980 --> 00:29:21,620
What?

491
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,880
Didn't you say you'd already
rescheduled the client's meeting?

492
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:26,220
Just because I rescheduled it

493
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:28,280
doesn't mean
I don't have to go home, you know.

494
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:32,240
But you're the one who told me that

495
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:34,940
a sick person shouldn't be left alone.

496
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:39,520
But you seem better now.

497
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:48,260
Just because I'm feeling better

498
00:29:48,280 --> 00:29:50,240
doesn't mean I'm fully recovered.

499
00:29:50,620 --> 00:29:52,680
With you here last night,

500
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:54,360
I went to bed early

501
00:29:54,520 --> 00:29:56,760
and got a full eight hours of sleep.

502
00:29:58,280 --> 00:29:59,280
Good for you.

503
00:29:59,880 --> 00:30:01,040
Well...

504
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:03,080
why don't we share a bed every night?

505
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,620
Are you gonna leave
a sick person alone like this?

506
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:18,100
What if I fall and hit my head on the floor?

507
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:19,720
Aren't you even worried about me?

508
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:22,680
I'm just going back to grab some clothes

509
00:30:22,700 --> 00:30:24,320
and a few things real quick.

510
00:30:24,680 --> 00:30:26,180
If you can't be on your own,

511
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:27,280
there's nothing I can do.

512
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,800
So, that means you'll be back, right?

513
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:33,040
I'll try to be back before noon, then.

514
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:35,240
Let me know if you want anything to eat.

515
00:30:35,260 --> 00:30:36,640
I'll grab it on my way back.

516
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,560
I want to eat...

517
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:43,400
Anything is fine,

518
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:46,320
as long as I get to eat with you.

519
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,440
[Topknot Kuman]

520
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:17,760
Are you here already?

521
00:31:21,480 --> 00:31:22,560
- Hi!
- Hi!

522
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,040
"Mim, Oyl, come on in."

523
00:31:28,060 --> 00:31:29,100
Alright, Soul.

524
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:30,800
Gosh, I'm starving.

525
00:31:36,440 --> 00:31:38,040
Xinxin, come on in.

526
00:31:39,600 --> 00:31:41,620
I haven't seen you in a while, Ms. Xinxin...

527
00:31:41,640 --> 00:31:43,280
You look even cuter.

528
00:31:46,160 --> 00:31:47,560
- Wow...
- Right.

529
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:52,240
Well,

530
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:54,400
I'm glad you can...

531
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:56,520
still remember my name.

532
00:31:57,560 --> 00:31:58,660
Of course,

533
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,580
Mr. Boy.

534
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:02,600
Uh...

535
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:04,320
It's "Oyl,"

536
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:05,440
not "Boy."

537
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:06,320
Oh...

538
00:32:07,100 --> 00:32:08,920
I'm sorry, Mr. Oyl.

539
00:32:09,400 --> 00:32:10,500
Well, I...

540
00:32:10,520 --> 00:32:13,080
have trouble remembering people's names.

541
00:32:14,960 --> 00:32:16,120
It's okay.

542
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,180
No wonder

543
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,040
you keep...

544
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:20,380
calling Soul

545
00:32:20,400 --> 00:32:21,680
"Miss Architect."

546
00:32:22,060 --> 00:32:23,240
So that's why.

547
00:32:24,360 --> 00:32:25,000
Hey.

548
00:32:25,500 --> 00:32:26,680
Don't you have anything better to do today?

549
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:27,960
Got plenty of free time, Soul.

550
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:29,600
Like, I'm free all day.

551
00:32:29,760 --> 00:32:30,920
I'll assign you some work, then,

552
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,760
- What?
- to keep you busy.

553
00:32:33,040 --> 00:32:34,560
Come on, Soul.

554
00:32:34,700 --> 00:32:35,900
You should be touched

555
00:32:35,920 --> 00:32:38,000
that we came all this way to visit you.

556
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:39,320
Hey...

557
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:42,000
if you already have
someone to look after you,

558
00:32:42,020 --> 00:32:43,440
I think I should head back for now.

559
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:44,520
Hey...

560
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,200
Uh...

561
00:32:49,560 --> 00:32:51,600
Oyl and I are heading back now, Ms. Xinxin.

562
00:32:51,720 --> 00:32:52,320
Huh?

563
00:32:52,520 --> 00:32:55,340
We were just passing by, so we thought
we'd stop by and check on Soul.

564
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:57,900
- Come on, Oyl. Let's head back.
- Huh?!

565
00:32:57,920 --> 00:32:59,860
Hey, I still wanna stay.

566
00:32:59,880 --> 00:33:01,080
I haven't seen Ms. Xinxin in so long.

567
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:03,260
There's still a ton of work to do,
and you're just chilling.

568
00:33:03,280 --> 00:33:05,120
Should I have the boss call you in?

569
00:33:05,140 --> 00:33:05,840
Come on.

570
00:33:05,980 --> 00:33:06,960
- Hey.
- Get up!

571
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:08,620
We'll get going now, Soul.

572
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:11,140
Please take care of her too, Ms. Xinxin.

573
00:33:11,160 --> 00:33:12,580
Come on, let's go!

574
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:15,080
See you later, Ms. Xinxin. See you!

575
00:33:15,100 --> 00:33:16,700
See you, Mr. Boy.

576
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,460
- It's Oyl. Oyl.
- Right, Mr. Oyl.

577
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:19,680
Yes, Mr. Oyl.

578
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:22,520
I'll leave him to you, Mim.

579
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:29,180
You're not coughing anymore?

580
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:30,860
Coughing...

581
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:31,440
Oh.

582
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:35,800
Ugh...

583
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,360
Miss Architect.

584
00:33:54,280 --> 00:33:54,920
Hm?

585
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:58,540
Stop working and just get some rest already.

586
00:33:58,560 --> 00:34:00,360
I'll wake you up in the evening.

587
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:03,960
Just a little bit more.

588
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:05,640
Please?

589
00:34:07,080 --> 00:34:09,240
You said you were gonna be good, didn't you?

590
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:19,740
What is it?

591
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:22,960
You told me to get some rest,

592
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:24,360
so I'm gonna rest.

593
00:34:25,720 --> 00:34:26,840
Where?

594
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,400
Right here.

595
00:34:31,640 --> 00:34:34,000
I meant you should go rest in your room.

596
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:36,080
Can I sleep here, please?

597
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:37,840
Just for a little while.

598
00:35:21,580 --> 00:35:23,200
When did I fall asleep?

599
00:35:24,640 --> 00:35:25,800
Are you up?

600
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:28,920
Was I being too loud?

601
00:35:40,520 --> 00:35:42,720
The last thing I remember,

602
00:35:43,200 --> 00:35:44,480
you were the one asleep.

603
00:35:45,040 --> 00:35:47,160
Then why did I

604
00:35:47,280 --> 00:35:48,720
end up being the one awake?

605
00:35:49,720 --> 00:35:51,260
When I woke up,

606
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:54,360
I saw you sleeping with your head
drooping like a rag doll.

607
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:56,600
So, I just let you sleep.

608
00:35:57,120 --> 00:35:58,720
Stop exaggerating.

609
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,280
Oh? You don't believe me, huh?

610
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:05,130
What?

611
00:36:05,430 --> 00:36:05,980
Hey.

612
00:36:06,240 --> 00:36:07,030
I looked ugly.

613
00:36:07,590 --> 00:36:08,360
Come on, delete it!

614
00:36:08,670 --> 00:36:09,550
Delete it!

615
00:36:10,090 --> 00:36:11,020
But you were cute in this.

616
00:36:11,580 --> 00:36:13,140
Hey, delete it!

617
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:16,700
Alright, alright.

618
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:18,120
I'll delete it for you.

619
00:36:18,520 --> 00:36:20,760
But I'm hungry now,

620
00:36:21,360 --> 00:36:22,760
so let's eat something first.

621
00:36:35,240 --> 00:36:37,400
I'm getting tired of congee and rice soup.

622
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:39,280
Can you eat these?

623
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:42,760
Mm.

624
00:36:44,860 --> 00:36:46,560
It's been a week, you know.

625
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:50,360
What?

626
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,800
We haven't eaten together like this

627
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:56,480
since that day at the restaurant.

628
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:01,900
Well, who has the time for that?

629
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:06,680
Then, how about we

630
00:37:07,080 --> 00:37:08,360
go out for a meal this Sunday?

631
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:13,200
But they won't be around this Sunday.

632
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:15,120
Auntie Tai and my mom
won't be back by then.

633
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:18,520
This isn't about them.

634
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:21,160
I meant just you and me.

635
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:23,120
Let's have a meal, just the two of us.

636
00:37:25,120 --> 00:37:27,080
Just the two of us?

637
00:37:27,460 --> 00:37:28,240
Mm.

638
00:37:29,300 --> 00:37:30,160
Wanna go with me?

639
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:34,200
Miss Architect.

640
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:37,680
Yes?

641
00:37:40,060 --> 00:37:41,440
What you're doing right now...

642
00:37:42,200 --> 00:37:43,880
are you trying to hit on me?

643
00:37:49,540 --> 00:37:51,560
If I hit on you,

644
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:53,440
would you be okay with that?

645
00:37:55,960 --> 00:37:59,720
Since you brought it up, I...

646
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:02,240
Eat it. Eat all of it.

647
00:38:45,020 --> 00:38:46,400
You couldn't sleep?

648
00:38:47,620 --> 00:38:48,720
Mm...

649
00:38:49,260 --> 00:38:51,640
Probably because
I took a nap this evening.

650
00:38:53,300 --> 00:38:55,140
Did I wake you up?

651
00:39:05,220 --> 00:39:06,640
What do you usually do

652
00:39:06,900 --> 00:39:08,720
when you can't sleep?

653
00:39:13,140 --> 00:39:14,240
Maybe watch a movie.

654
00:39:14,820 --> 00:39:16,160
You like watching movies?

655
00:39:17,300 --> 00:39:18,100
Mm...

656
00:39:20,340 --> 00:39:21,870
What kind do you like?

657
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:23,390
Romance?

658
00:39:24,100 --> 00:39:25,470
Or horror?

659
00:39:26,740 --> 00:39:28,110
I'm scared of ghosts.

660
00:39:29,380 --> 00:39:30,190
Hm?

661
00:39:32,260 --> 00:39:34,910
So you're into romance movies.

662
00:39:38,340 --> 00:39:39,310
What about you?

663
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:42,760
Mm...

664
00:39:44,020 --> 00:39:45,790
I'm not really a movie person,

665
00:39:46,580 --> 00:39:48,510
especially at the cinema.

666
00:39:49,060 --> 00:39:51,670
The last one I saw was probably...

667
00:39:53,300 --> 00:39:54,910
ten years ago, I think.

668
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:59,450
I bet you watched it with your ex.

669
00:40:02,560 --> 00:40:04,880
What's with Thai people and their exes?

670
00:40:07,700 --> 00:40:08,720
I know, right?

671
00:40:11,580 --> 00:40:13,360
Well, I did go see it with my ex,

672
00:40:13,380 --> 00:40:15,840
but it was a long time ago.

673
00:40:15,860 --> 00:40:17,390
I don't remember much now.

674
00:40:19,700 --> 00:40:20,830
So...

675
00:40:21,900 --> 00:40:24,400
have you been single ever since?

676
00:40:26,140 --> 00:40:28,960
How come you've been single for so long?

677
00:40:31,900 --> 00:40:34,750
Well...I'm in no rush.

678
00:40:36,540 --> 00:40:37,680
What about you, Xinxin?

679
00:40:38,340 --> 00:40:40,760
Auntie Phing told me that...

680
00:40:40,780 --> 00:40:42,600
you've never dated anyone.

681
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:44,520
Don't you ever want to be in love?

682
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:48,040
Of course I do.

683
00:40:49,500 --> 00:40:51,750
Everyone wants to be in love.

684
00:40:53,340 --> 00:40:55,550
I think it'd be nice...

685
00:40:56,100 --> 00:40:57,960
to be loved,

686
00:40:58,740 --> 00:41:00,080
or to love someone.

687
00:41:01,940 --> 00:41:03,840
But I'm not in a rush.

688
00:41:04,740 --> 00:41:06,800
I'm only 25.

689
00:41:09,820 --> 00:41:11,710
I'm only 29 myself.

690
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:14,400
But my mom...wow,

691
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:16,080
she's really eager for me to find someone.

692
00:41:16,340 --> 00:41:17,280
It's like

693
00:41:18,100 --> 00:41:19,140
I'm going to die

694
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:20,500
as soon as I turn 30.

695
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:25,960
But...

696
00:41:26,620 --> 00:41:28,840
I believe in timing, though.

697
00:41:29,700 --> 00:41:30,900
If you're meant

698
00:41:31,300 --> 00:41:32,760
to find someone,

699
00:41:33,320 --> 00:41:35,040
it'll happen eventually.

700
00:41:41,740 --> 00:41:43,390
Then why did you buy me that lamp?

701
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:48,310
Well...

702
00:41:49,460 --> 00:41:52,240
it's meant to ward off bad luck.

703
00:41:53,620 --> 00:41:55,360
And why did you believe me?

704
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:58,920
I didn't believe you.

705
00:41:59,780 --> 00:42:01,920
I just didn't want to upset you.

706
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:08,600
You're actually pretty nice, huh?

707
00:42:10,340 --> 00:42:12,040
You just realized that?

708
00:42:19,200 --> 00:42:20,280
Uh...

709
00:42:21,880 --> 00:42:23,800
Can I ask you something?

710
00:42:25,780 --> 00:42:26,680
Hm?

711
00:42:29,860 --> 00:42:30,960
Let's say...

712
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:32,000
Like...

713
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:34,920
Let's say...

714
00:42:35,480 --> 00:42:37,160
when we really like someone,

715
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:40,650
what does it feel like?

716
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:43,080
Like, I mean...

717
00:42:43,940 --> 00:42:45,880
How would we know?

718
00:42:49,500 --> 00:42:51,320
Just listen to your heart.

719
00:42:54,340 --> 00:42:55,380
How so?

720
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:04,560
Come on, get up.

721
00:43:10,820 --> 00:43:13,360
Try placing your hand
on your heart, like this.

722
00:43:19,200 --> 00:43:20,240
Do you feel anything?

723
00:43:21,920 --> 00:43:22,920
It's beating.

724
00:43:24,240 --> 00:43:26,560
Well, of course it's beating.

725
00:43:30,200 --> 00:43:31,240
What do you feel?

726
00:43:38,860 --> 00:43:39,980
I...

727
00:43:40,540 --> 00:43:41,600
feel...

728
00:43:44,820 --> 00:43:46,520
Feel what?

729
00:43:51,220 --> 00:43:52,600
My heart is racing.

730
00:44:00,660 --> 00:44:01,880
Just like that.

731
00:44:07,860 --> 00:44:09,720
If you like someone,

732
00:44:10,520 --> 00:44:12,360
your heart will race

733
00:44:12,740 --> 00:44:14,360
when you're near them.

734
00:44:55,540 --> 00:44:57,120
Sweet dreams, Xinxin.

735
00:45:15,420 --> 00:45:17,680
I think I really like Xinxin.

736
00:45:17,740 --> 00:45:19,160
She finally admitted it.

737
00:45:20,240 --> 00:45:21,160
You knew?

738
00:45:21,440 --> 00:45:22,500
Gosh, Soul.

739
00:45:22,520 --> 00:45:24,040
It's this obvious.

740
00:45:24,060 --> 00:45:25,240
So, what's next?

741
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:26,620
Have you told her you like her?

742
00:45:26,640 --> 00:45:27,880
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

743
00:45:30,280 --> 00:45:31,580
- What?
- Gosh...

744
00:45:31,600 --> 00:45:32,880
What the heck, Soul?

745
00:45:33,220 --> 00:45:35,800
You're nothing like the lady-killer
Ms. Xinxin said you were.

746
00:45:37,160 --> 00:45:38,361
How can she act like nothing's going on

747
00:45:38,373 --> 00:45:40,080
when I'm being this obvious?

748
00:45:40,420 --> 00:45:41,940
She didn't respond

749
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:43,640
to anything I said.

750
00:45:44,460 --> 00:45:47,120
Well, you haven't told her
you like her yet.

751
00:45:47,580 --> 00:45:49,680
- Maybe she's not sure yet.
- Mm.

752
00:45:49,840 --> 00:45:51,300
If you like someone, just tell them.

753
00:45:51,320 --> 00:45:53,100
Love isn't that complicated, Soul.

754
00:45:53,120 --> 00:45:54,280
- She's right!
- Mm.

755
00:45:56,100 --> 00:45:58,980
And did Ms. Lada say anything

756
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:00,280
to you about Xinxin, Mim?

757
00:46:01,120 --> 00:46:02,520
No, she didn't.

758
00:46:02,640 --> 00:46:03,920
Hey, wait, wait, wait.

759
00:46:04,320 --> 00:46:05,320
Lada...

760
00:46:05,340 --> 00:46:08,380
You mean Ms. Lada, who talks to you
about work all the time?

761
00:46:08,680 --> 00:46:10,080
Why her?

762
00:46:10,360 --> 00:46:11,400
You didn't know?

763
00:46:12,080 --> 00:46:12,760
Hey.

764
00:46:13,360 --> 00:46:14,220
I didn't.

765
00:46:14,240 --> 00:46:15,920
So, what do you guys even know?

766
00:46:16,260 --> 00:46:18,800
Hey, how could you not tell me, Soul?!

767
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:20,737
We're partners. We're on the same team.

768
00:46:20,742 --> 00:46:21,950
Come on, Soul, tell me.

769
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:23,400
Gosh!

770
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:25,360
Lada and I are dating!

771
00:46:25,390 --> 00:46:26,250
- What?!
- Period!

772
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:28,880
You?!

773
00:46:30,080 --> 00:46:31,960
Gosh, I'm shocked!

774
00:46:32,460 --> 00:46:34,180
That Lada and I are dating?

775
00:46:34,200 --> 00:46:36,330
No, that I'm the only one still single.

776
00:46:36,840 --> 00:46:39,160
- Ugh...
- Come on. I'm single, too.

777
00:46:39,800 --> 00:46:41,671
If you don't make a move,

778
00:46:41,683 --> 00:46:42,800
you'll stay single for sure.

779
00:46:43,320 --> 00:46:44,740
Then what do you want me to do?

780
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:47,140
She snuck back home early
yesterday morning.

781
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:48,320
I've called and texted her,

782
00:46:48,340 --> 00:46:50,360
but she still hasn't replied.

783
00:46:51,080 --> 00:46:52,900
So, what did you do to her?

784
00:46:52,920 --> 00:46:53,540
Yeah.

785
00:46:53,560 --> 00:46:55,120
Don't tell me...

786
00:46:56,740 --> 00:46:58,240
I didn't do anything.

787
00:46:58,460 --> 00:47:00,100
Well, I just...

788
00:47:00,120 --> 00:47:01,370
- Just?
- Just?

789
00:47:02,640 --> 00:47:04,020
I just asked her

790
00:47:04,040 --> 00:47:06,680
if she'd be okay with me hitting on her.

791
00:47:07,880 --> 00:47:10,260
- Gosh, I'm swooning.
- Ow, that hurts!

792
00:47:10,280 --> 00:47:11,610
Oh, I'm sorry.

793
00:47:12,680 --> 00:47:14,240
But she didn't respond.

794
00:47:14,340 --> 00:47:16,240
She didn't say yes,
but she didn't say no either.

795
00:47:16,300 --> 00:47:18,820
- That means you still have a chance.
- Mm, true.

796
00:47:18,840 --> 00:47:19,738
Then go.

797
00:47:19,750 --> 00:47:21,280
- Get off work right now.
- Go, go, go.

798
00:47:21,300 --> 00:47:22,220
Go where?

799
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:25,060
- Gosh, Soul.
- Go see Xinxin!

800
00:47:25,080 --> 00:47:26,120
- Yeah.
- Go!

801
00:47:26,140 --> 00:47:28,360
Been smart for half the series,
then suddenly gone so dumb?!

802
00:47:31,020 --> 00:47:32,020
Hurry.

803
00:47:32,040 --> 00:47:34,154
Alright, here's your bag.

804
00:47:34,166 --> 00:47:35,200
Go on, open the door.

805
00:47:35,640 --> 00:47:36,380
Off you go!

806
00:47:42,740 --> 00:47:43,640
Finally.

807
00:47:43,740 --> 00:47:44,760
Took her so long to admit it.

808
00:47:49,460 --> 00:47:50,800
"So, can I?"

809
00:47:51,200 --> 00:47:52,700
If you weren't that important,

810
00:47:52,720 --> 00:47:54,700
she wouldn't leave her meeting
just to see you.

811
00:47:54,710 --> 00:47:55,430
Am I right?

812
00:47:56,520 --> 00:48:00,290
You're not the only architect
in this world, you know.

813
00:48:02,240 --> 00:48:04,780
But the only feng shui master
I want to work with

814
00:48:06,280 --> 00:48:07,560
is you, Xinxin.

815
00:48:11,120 --> 00:48:13,520
I meant you should go rest in your room.

816
00:48:13,800 --> 00:48:15,560
Can I sleep here, please?

817
00:48:15,880 --> 00:48:17,280
Just for a little while.

818
00:48:20,980 --> 00:48:23,600
Try placing your hand
on your heart, like this.

819
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:29,850
I...

820
00:48:30,500 --> 00:48:31,640
feel...

821
00:48:33,840 --> 00:48:35,320
Oh my gosh!

822
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:37,520
Who's there?

823
00:49:00,280 --> 00:49:01,160
What?

824
00:49:01,600 --> 00:49:02,760
So you're home, huh?

825
00:49:04,120 --> 00:49:06,760
Why didn't you call first
before coming over?

826
00:49:08,060 --> 00:49:09,760
And you answered my calls?

827
00:49:13,320 --> 00:49:15,080
I bought a lot of food,

828
00:49:15,600 --> 00:49:16,880
but I can't finish it all by myself.

829
00:49:17,720 --> 00:49:18,760
Have some with me.

830
00:49:21,520 --> 00:49:22,500
Please?

831
00:49:39,760 --> 00:49:41,080
Were you avoiding me on purpose?

832
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:43,880
No, I wasn't.

833
00:49:44,440 --> 00:49:46,880
It's not like I was avoiding you.

834
00:49:47,840 --> 00:49:49,020
Xinxin, you're a terrible liar,

835
00:49:49,040 --> 00:49:50,600
you know that?

836
00:49:51,480 --> 00:49:52,320
And...

837
00:49:52,920 --> 00:49:54,880
how did you know I was lying?

838
00:49:55,880 --> 00:49:57,420
Whenever you lie,

839
00:49:57,440 --> 00:49:58,560
your nose flares.

840
00:50:02,080 --> 00:50:02,880
Really?

841
00:50:04,040 --> 00:50:04,880
See?

842
00:50:04,900 --> 00:50:06,440
You really lied to me.

843
00:50:11,000 --> 00:50:11,920
So?

844
00:50:12,400 --> 00:50:13,400
Tell me.

845
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:16,480
Why were you avoiding me?

846
00:50:16,750 --> 00:50:18,080
Don't talk to me like that.

847
